<title>USA: Trident to buy back 250,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Trident to buy back 250,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>BROOKFIELD, Conn. 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trident International Inc said Thursday that its board of directors has voted to authorize the company to purchase up to 250,000 shares of its common stock.</p>
<p>The company said the purhcases would be made from time to time on the open market as market conditions warrant and would be used to adjust its capital structure, to meet its obligations under its employee benefit plans, and for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>Trident makes a proprietary impulse inkjet technology for industrial original equipment manufacturers.</p>
</text>
